
== §1 — NO DESIGN, NO CALCULATION, NO CODE ==
  ✓ the MEP spec names no MEP standard
  ✓ regulatory rule count is still zero
  ✓ real occupancy classification count is still zero
  ✓ browser spec is byte-identical to acs_mep.json
  ✓ seven MEP element types declared
  ✓ twenty-five system types declared
  ✓ DESIGNED / COMPLIANT / ADEQUATE / BALANCED / CALCULATED are not model statuses
  ✓ UNSAFE / CODE_VIOLATION / FIRE_VIOLATION are not severities
  ✓ OPTIMIZED is not a routing status
  ✓ rule and code_required are not provenance values
  ✓ no compiled MEP element carries a load, flow, size-calc or compliance field
  ✓ no compiled output uses MEP-compliance language
  ✓ the language actually used is representational

== §2 — NO SYSTEM IS INFERRED FROM BUILDING TYPE ==
  ✓ a villa gets no sprinkler system it did not declare
  ✓ a hotel gets no emergency power it did not declare
  ✓ a warehouse gets no fire-water system it did not declare
  ✓ a model with no MEP block produces no MEP element
  ✓ and that model is still perfectly valid
  ✓ every system present is present because the fixture declared it
  ✓ the same compiler serves every programme

== §3 — PROVENANCE AND STATUS ==
  ✓ every element records a provenance from the declared vocabulary
  ✓ test_fixture and system_default are not verified sources
  ✓ an undeclared status is derived, never assumed
  ✓ the model is never marked regulatory
  ✓ synthetic fixtures declare themselves synthetic

== §4 — SYSTEMS, DISCIPLINES AND MEDIA ==
  ✓ five villa systems compile
  ✓ each system maps to a declared discipline
  ✓ lighting is separated from general power for display
  ✓ a medium is carried as a factual label
  ✓ a medium attaches no pressure or flow assumption
  ✓ an unknown system type is reported and mapped to OTHER
  ✓ an unknown medium is reported, not invented

== §5 — NODES, SEGMENTS AND ROUTING ==
  ✓ seven villa nodes compile
  ✓ a node takes its elevation from the architectural level table
  ✓ a node carries no capacity
  ✓ a routed segment keeps its supplied polyline
  ✓ its length is measured from the polyline, not assumed
  ✓ a segment with endpoints but no geometry stays UNROUTED
  ✓ and NO path is fabricated for it
  ✓ the unrouted state is reported as INFO with an explicit reason
  ✓ the relationship layer says UNROUTED rather than inventing a connection
  ✓ a vertical riser segment is representable in real XYZ

== §6 — DISPLAY FALLBACK IS NEVER AN ENGINEERING VALUE ==
  ✓ a segment with no stated size keeps size=null
  ✓ but still yields render geometry
  ✓ and that geometry is labelled display_fallback
  ✓ the fallback never reaches the rule inputs
  ✓ a sized segment is model-sourced instead
  ✓ equipment with no dimensions draws from a fallback, flagged as such
  ✓ the spec states the fallback policy in writing
  ✓ compiling does not write a fallback back into the model
  ✓ no invented voltage, breaker, flow, head or capacity appears in any field

== §7 — EQUIPMENT, TERMINALS AND PORTS ==
  ✓ equipment types come from the declared list
  ✓ no rating, capacity or duty is produced
  ✓ a stated property is kept with its own provenance
  ✓ ports are recorded only where declared
  ✓ an unrecognised port type is reported, not accepted
  ✓ plumbing fixtures are represented as terminals, not a parallel model
  ✓ air devices are represented as terminals too
  ✓ no CFM, L/s, throw or neck size is fabricated for an air device
  ✓ an unrecognised terminal type is reported

== §8 — PHASE 1 ADAPTER PRESERVES PROVENANCE ==
  ✓ Phase 1 points are adapted into represented terminals
  ✓ the adapter creates no duplicate semantic object — each names its origin point
  ✓ a system-generated smoke detector stays system_default
  ✓ a user-supplied point keeps its user provenance
  ✓ NO adapted terminal is ever raised to a code requirement
  ✓ code_required is not even a value the adapter could write
  ✓ a light point becomes a light fixture, not a lighting design
  ✓ the adapter can be turned off and changes nothing else
  ✓ the original model is not modified by adaptation

== §9 — RISERS AND SHAFT ASSOCIATION ==
  ✓ four risers compile across three levels
  ✓ a riser spanning levels emits RISER_CONNECTS_LEVELS
  ✓ an architectural core is NOT an MEP riser by itself
  ✓ the one declared association records its evidence source
  ✓ the spec states the rule in writing
  ✓ a riser outside the core it names is reported
  ✓ an unresolvable riser level is an ERROR

== §10 — RELATIONSHIPS ARE NOT SERVICE ADEQUACY ==
  ✓ every relationship type is in the declared vocabulary
  ✓ every relationship carries the no-adequacy note
  ✓ a terminal in a room yields SYSTEM_HAS_TERMINAL_IN with an explicit disclaimer
  ✓ SYSTEM_SERVES_SPACE says representation only
  ✓ no relationship claims a room receives adequate anything
  ✓ circuits are never grouped automatically
  ✓ a declared circuit IS represented when the model supplies one
  ✓ relationship ids are unique and namespaced

== §11 — ARCHITECTURAL AND STRUCTURAL INTERFERENCE ==
  ✓ a duct crossing a wall with no penetration is reported
  ✓ a pipe crossing a slab with no penetration is reported
  ✓ a segment crossing a structural beam is reported
  ✓ a segment crossing a structural column is reported
  ✓ equipment outside its assigned space is reported
  ✓ a terminal outside its assigned space is reported
  ✓ a route leaving the building footprint is reported
  ✓ an MEP element inside a stair void is reported
  ✓ every interference is a model-quality severity, never a code verdict
  ✓ a beam clash says the member is not cut and the route is not redesigned
  ✓ no clash modifies the architectural model
  ✓ no clash modifies the structural model
  ✓ a declared penetration suppresses the crossing report at that host

== §12 — PENETRATIONS INFER NOTHING ==
  ✓ a declared penetration compiles and resolves its host
  ✓ it infers no fire stopping, sleeve or reinforcement
  ✓ the spec repeats the rule
  ✓ an unresolvable penetration host is reported
  ✓ an unresolvable penetration segment is an ERROR
  ✓ PENETRATION_THROUGH is a factual edge only

== §13 — FIRE SYSTEMS ARE DATA ONLY ==
  ✓ a fire alarm system is representable
  ✓ smoke detectors are represented as terminals
  ✓ no coverage, spacing, zoning or hydraulic field exists anywhere
  ✓ the spec states there is no fire/life-safety engine
  ✓ the compiled model repeats it
  ✓ sprinkler and fire-water are declarable but never auto-created
  ✓ no fire element carries a compliance or evaluation verdict

== §14 — LOW CURRENT / ICT ==
  ✓ a data network system is representable
  ✓ a data outlet is a represented terminal
  ✓ no coverage or network design is produced
  ✓ CCTV, Wi-Fi, access control, intercom and BMS are all representable types

== §15 — CLINIC MEDICAL GAS IS EXPLICITLY SYNTHETIC ==
  ✓ the medical gas system is present only because the fixture declares it
  ✓ it is clearly labelled test-only and synthetic
  ✓ no healthcare compliance is implied anywhere
  ✓ the only mentions of compliance are explicit denials

== §16 — INTEGRITY VALIDATION ==
  ✓ the deliberately broken fixture triggers every integrity check
  ✓ every issue code is declared in the spec with a severity
  ✓ issues are ordered ERROR first, then WARNING, then INFO
  ✓ no issue is a code-compliance verdict
  ✓ an unknown MEP collection is reported and NOT interpreted
  ✓ a foreign building id is caught rather than silently re-namespaced
  ✓ a NaN coordinate is rejected rather than propagated

== §17 — DETERMINISM, NAMESPACING AND TRANSFORMS ==
  ✓ compiling twice gives byte-identical output
  ✓ the compiler never mutates the model it reads
  ✓ a second building namespaces every MEP id
  ✓ two buildings can never collide on an id
  ✓ a space reference belonging to another building is caught, not silently accepted
  ✓ a transform never changes the compiled geometry
  ✓ the building transform is applied on read
  ✓ rotation is applied about the building origin
  ✓ no second coordinate convention is introduced

== §18 — REVISION HASH ==
  ✓ moving equipment changes the model hash
  ✓ changing a pipe route changes the model hash
  ✓ adding duct route geometry changes the model hash
  ✓ removing a terminal changes the model hash
  ✓ changing a system property changes the model hash
  ✓ adding a riser changes the model hash
  ✓ toggling layer visibility does NOT change the model hash
  ✓ moving the camera still does not change the hash
  ✓ compiling the MEP model does not change the hash

== §19 — RENDER AND EXPORT ==
  ✓ render items use the MEP| naming convention
  ✓ each discipline requested by the phase has its own display layer
  ✓ the fire layer name says data only, with no safety engine
  ✓ every render item declares where its geometry came from
  ✓ render items never carry an engineering verdict
  ✓ colour marks the discipline only, never a state
  ✓ an unrouted segment produces no render geometry

== §20 — RULE ENGINE CONTRACT (INPUTS ONLY) ==
  ✓ system existence is exposed as a factual input
  ✓ terminal and equipment counts are exposed
  ✓ segment size is exposed only when it is real
  ✓ serves_space is exposed as a factual relation
  ✓ no regulatory rule was added anywhere
  ✓ the rule inputs contain no threshold, limit or verdict

== §21 — NO ARCHITECTURAL / STRUCTURAL / NAV / EGRESS REGRESSION ==
  ✓ adding an MEP block changes no architectural element
  ✓ adding an MEP block changes no structural element
  ✓ relationships are identical with and without the MEP block
  ✓ navigation is identical with and without the MEP block
